<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-model href="http://www.tei-c.org/release/xml/tei/custom/schema/relaxng/tei_odds.rng" type="application/xml" schematypens="http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:lang="en">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Common Ground entries: TEI customisation</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <publisher>Common Ground (historicalesque/carlton)</publisher>
        <p>Source of the schema in <ref target="carlton.rng">schema/carlton.rng</ref>. Edit this file, then regenerate the schema as described in the README.</p>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>Written for the site; based on TEI P5.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <head>Common Ground entries</head>

      <div xml:id="intro">
        <head>What an entry is</head>
        <p>Each entry on the site is one TEI file in <ident>civic/</ident>. Its <gi>TEI</gi> element says what
          the entry is about in <att>type</att>: a <val>person</val>, an <val>org</val> (a business or organisation,
          such as a hotel or brewery), a <val>family</val>, a <val>place</val> (a street, building or area) or a
          <val>topic</val> (such as cesspits or street numbering).</p>
        <p>An entry has three parts:</p>
        <list>
          <item><gi>teiHeader</gi>: the title, the authors, the sources the authors used (<gi>sourceDesc</gi>/<gi>listBibl</gi>),
            and one <gi>change</gi> in <gi>revisionDesc</gi> for each contribution or edit.</item>
          <item><gi>standOff</gi>: the structured facts about the subject. A person goes in <gi>listPerson</gi>/<gi>person</gi>,
            a family in <gi>listPerson</gi>/<gi>personGrp</gi>, a business in <gi>listOrg</gi>/<gi>org</gi> and a place in
            <gi>listPlace</gi>/<gi>place</gi>, with <att>xml:id</att> <val>subject</val>. Topics have no subject record.
            Dated events go in <gi>listEvent</gi> (shown as the Chronology) and links to other entries in <gi>listRelation</gi>.</item>
          <item><gi>text</gi>/<gi>body</gi>: the article. Each heading starts a new <gi>div</gi>.</item>
        </list>
        <p>Dates use <att>when</att>, <att>from</att> and <att>to</att> with ISO values (a year is enough), and
          <att>cert</att> <val>low</val> when the contributor marked them as approximate.</p>
      </div>

      <div xml:id="schema">
        <head>Schema</head>
        <schemaSpec ident="carlton" start="TEI" prefix="tei_" docLang="en">
          <moduleRef key="tei"/>
          <moduleRef key="core"/>
          <moduleRef key="header"/>
          <moduleRef key="textstructure"/>
          <moduleRef key="namesdates"/>
          <moduleRef key="linking"/>
          <moduleRef key="figures"/>

          <!-- What the entry is about -->
          <elementSpec ident="TEI" mode="change">
            <attList>
              <attDef ident="type" mode="change" usage="req">
                <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
                  <valItem ident="person"><desc>A person.</desc></valItem>
                  <valItem ident="org"><desc>A business or organisation, such as a hotel, brewery, school or society.</desc></valItem>
                  <valItem ident="family"><desc>A family.</desc></valItem>
                  <valItem ident="place"><desc>A place: a street, building, block or area.</desc></valItem>
                  <valItem ident="topic"><desc>A topic, such as cesspits or street numbering.</desc></valItem>
                  <valItem ident="unknown"><desc>The contributor didn't say. Editors should change it before accepting.</desc></valItem>
                </valList>
              </attDef>
            </attList>
          </elementSpec>

          <!-- Text styles the contribution form produces -->
          <elementSpec ident="hi" mode="change">
            <attList>
              <attDef ident="rend" mode="change">
                <valList type="semi" mode="add">
                  <valItem ident="italic"/>
                  <valItem ident="bold"/>
                  <valItem ident="underline"/>
                </valList>
              </attDef>
            </attList>
          </elementSpec>

          <elementSpec ident="list" mode="change">
            <attList>
              <attDef ident="rend" mode="change">
                <valList type="semi" mode="add">
                  <valItem ident="bulleted"/>
                  <valItem ident="numbered"/>
                </valList>
              </attDef>
            </attList>
          </elementSpec>
        </schemaSpec>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
</TEI>
